Tsunderplane is one of those cards that got changed very early, which ended up lost. This is because Tsunderplane originally restored 5 HP to its owner upon death, making it an upgraded version of [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Vegetoid Vegetoid], but was nerfed to only healing 3 HP at some point (either undocumented or still before Alpha 2.1).

'''Beta 1.6''' changed it again, making us know its history clearly from now on. With this change, its entire use was swapped as it will now deal 1 DMG to all enemies upon death, making it more useful as both a powerful charge, but also a substitute of [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Woshua Woshua] that can also damage the enemy, an ability that is later given to [http://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Mettaton_NEO Mettaton NEO] as well.

This stayed for a very long time until '''Beta 31.2''', in which it was nerfed from an 8G Charge to a 9G Haste, but its effect was buffed in its place, dealing 2 more DMG to the opponent. '''Beta 32.0''' buffed its ATK from 5 to 6. This was brought down to 4 in '''Beta 41.1''', but its cost was also reduced by 2, to 7G.

